    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Margarethe Siems (20 December 1879 – 13 April 1952) was a German operatic soprano and voice teacher. A Kammersängerin of the Dresden State Opera, between 1909 and 1912 Siems created leading roles in three operas by Richard Strauss: Chrysothemis in \"Elektra\", the Marschallin in \"Der Rosenkavalier\", and Zerbinetta in \"Ariadne auf Naxos\".",
      "depth": 0,
