      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Karl Perron, born Karl Pergamenter and also known as Carl Perron, (3 June 1858 – 15 July 1928) was a German bass-baritone. A Kammersänger of the Dresden State Opera, he created leading roles in three operas by Richard Strauss – Jochanaan in \"Salome\", Orest in \"Elektra\", and Baron Ochs in \"Der Rosenkavalier\".",
